WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.711
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:14.439
Unit nine: Daily Schedule. Today you will describe your daily routine and habits.

4
00:00:14.739 --> 00:00:17.565
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.023
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:23.850
Routine.

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.535
Routine means the things you usually do every day.

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.428
My morning routine starts at six.

9
00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:33.460
Your turn. Say: Routine.

10
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.371
Routine.

11
00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:38.990
Punctual.

12
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:41.774
Punctual means always on time.

13
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:44.302
Our teacher is very punctual.

14
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:47.859
Your turn. Say: Punctual.

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.666
Punctual.

16
00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:53.383
Schedule.

17
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:57.021
Schedule means a plan of what you will do and when.

18
00:00:57.617 --> 00:00:59.686
My schedule is busy on Mondays.

19
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:02.796
Your turn. Say: Schedule.

20
00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:06.611
Schedule.

21
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.281
Deadline.

22
00:01:09.283 --> 00:01:12.270
Deadline means the last time or day to finish something.

23
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:15.092
The deadline for the project is Friday.

24
00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:18.092
Your turn. Say: Deadline.

25
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:22.120
Deadline.

26
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:23.699
Commute.

27
00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:27.356
Commute means the trip to school or work and back.

28
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.984
My commute takes twenty minutes.

29
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.038
Your turn. Say: Commute.

30
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:36.785
Commute.

31
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.609
Squeeze in.

32
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:42.406
Squeeze in means to find a little time for something.

33
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:45.353
I squeeze in some reading before bed.

34
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.300
Your turn. Say: Squeeze in.

35
00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:52.272
Squeeze in.

36
00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:54.111
Multitask.

37
00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:58.347
Multitask means to do several things at the same time.

38
00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.170
I can't multitask when I study.

39
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:04.854
Your turn. Say: Multitask.

40
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.806
Multitask.

41
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:10.389
Efficient.

42
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:14.277
Efficient means working well without wasting time.

43
00:02:14.883 --> 00:02:16.953
Making a list helps me be efficient.

44
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.632
Your turn. Say: Efficient.

45
00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.363
Efficient.

46
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:26.315
Procrastinate.

47
00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:30.303
Procrastinate means to delay doing something you should do.

48
00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.395
Don't procrastinate. Start now!

49
00:02:33.983 --> 00:02:36.845
Your turn. Say: Procrastinate.

50
00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.945
Procrastinate.

51
00:02:41.683 --> 00:02:42.928
Prioritize.

52
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.880
Prioritize means to do the most important things first.

53
00:02:47.483 --> 00:02:49.715
I prioritize homework every day.

54
00:02:50.317 --> 00:02:53.190
Your turn. Say: Prioritize.

55
00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.418
Prioritize.

56
00:02:58.183 --> 00:02:59.115
Balance.

57
00:03:00.117 --> 00:03:02.720
Balance means a good mix of different things.

58
00:03:03.317 --> 00:03:06.059
I try to keep a balance between study and fun.

59
00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.372
Your turn. Say: Balance.

60
00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:13.304
Balance.

61
00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.074
Organize.

62
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:19.093
Organize means to plan and arrange things in order.

63
00:03:19.683 --> 00:03:21.985
I organize my desk every evening.

64
00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:25.305
Your turn. Say: Organize.

65
00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.179
Organize.

66
00:03:29.967 --> 00:03:33.850
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:34.683 --> 00:03:36.648
Visal, what time do you wake up?

68
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.793
I wake up at six and leave home at half past six.

69
00:03:42.883 --> 00:03:44.395
How long is your commute?

70
00:03:45.483 --> 00:03:50.284
About twenty minutes by moto. I'm always punctual.

71
00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:52.953
When do you do your homework?

72
00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:59.068
I prioritize homework after school, then I squeeze in some games.

73
00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:02.268
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:06.150
Grammar focus: Present simple for habits.

75
00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.671
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:08.383 --> 00:04:09.802
I wake up at 6.

77
00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.914
I prioritize homework every day.

78
00:04:13.817 --> 00:04:16.211
She organizes her desk every evening.

79
00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:21.175
Add -s or -es with he, she or it: he watches, she goes, it starts.

80
00:04:21.917 --> 00:04:25.254
Be careful! Don't say: She wake up at six.

81
00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.362
Say: She wakes up at six.

82
00:04:29.662 --> 00:04:31.789
Add -s to the verb with he, she and it.

83
00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.345
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.390
My Busy Day.

85
00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.490
I try to be punctual and follow my daily routine.

86
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.881
I wake up at six, and my commute to school takes twenty minutes.

87
00:04:45.867 --> 00:04:49.782
After school, I prioritize my homework before the deadline.

88
00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:54.670
I don't procrastinate, and I don't multitask when I study.

89
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:59.199
In the evening, I squeeze in some free time to keep a good balance.

90
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.325
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:05.183 --> 00:05:07.160
She blank up at six every day.

92
00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.486
A, wakes. B, wake. C, waking.

93
00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.952
The answer is A: wakes.

94
00:05:17.117 --> 00:05:19.871
To delay doing something you should do is to blank.

95
00:05:20.171 --> 00:05:24.625
A, procrastinate. B, prioritize. C, organize.

96
00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:30.596
The answer is A: procrastinate.

97
00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.436
Always on time is blank.

98
00:05:33.736 --> 00:05:37.192
A, punctual. B, efficient. C, busy.

99
00:05:40.733 --> 00:05:42.919
The answer is A: punctual.

100
00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:47.366
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:48.217 --> 00:05:50.495
Describe your typical daily schedule.

102
00:05:59.283 --> 00:06:00.865
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:01.165 --> 00:06:10.911
I wake up at five thirty and go to school at six thirty. After school, I prioritize my homework, then I squeeze in some football.

104
00:06:11.211 --> 00:06:13.071
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:13.983 --> 00:06:18.540
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present simple for habits.

106
00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:23.094
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

107
00:06:23.394 --> 00:06:25.733
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

108
00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:28.883
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

